@startuml CU11_Generar_Backend_SpringBoot
title Communication Diagram — CU-11: Exportar Diagrama como Backend Spring Boot

' Objetos
object ":Usuario" as user
object ":DiagramPage\n(React)" as diagram
object ":export.js\n(API Client)" as exportApi
object ":AxiosClient" as axios
object ":ExportRouter\n(FastAPI)" as router
object ":Diagram\n(SQLAlchemy)" as diagramModel
object ":Clase / Atributo /\nMetodo / Relacion\n(ORM)" as orm
object ":PostgreSQL" as db
object ":uml_to_json\n(exporters)" as umlToJson
object ":validator\n(exporters)" as validator
object ":project_builder\n(exporters)" as builder
object ":json_to_full_orm" as genModels
object ":model_to_repository" as genRepos
object ":repository_to_service" as genServices
object ":service_to_controller" as genControllers
object ":model_to_dto" as genDtos
object ":postman_generator" as genPostman
object ":Jinja2\nTemplates" as templates
object ":FileSystem\n(output dir)" as fs

' === Flujo principal ===
user --> diagram : 1: click "Generar Backend"
diagram --> exportApi : 1.1: exportDownload(diagramId)
exportApi --> axios : 1.2: POST /diagrams/{id}/export-download
axios --> router : 1.3: HTTP POST
router --> diagramModel : 1.4: query(Diagram).filter(id)
diagramModel --> db : 1.5: SELECT diagram + JOIN\nclases, atributos, metodos, relaciones
db --> diagramModel : 1.6: full diagram data
router --> router : 1.7: build_diagram_dict(diagram)\n→ JSON normalizado

' === Pipeline de exportación ===
router --> umlToJson : 2: export_diagram_to_json(dict, path)
umlToJson --> umlToJson : 2.1: _normalize_diagram()\n→ PascalCase clases,\ncamelCase atributos,\nidentificadores Java válidos
umlToJson --> validator : 2.2: validate(diagram)\n→ check classes exist,\nrelations reference valid classes
validator --> umlToJson : 2.3: OK (or raise UMLValidationError)
umlToJson --> fs : 2.4: write diagram.json

router --> builder : 3: build_project(json_path, output_dir)

builder --> genModels : 3.1: generate_from_json()\n→ @Entity classes, @Id,\n@ManyToOne/@OneToMany/@ManyToMany,\n@JoinTable, cascades
genModels --> fs : 3.2: write Model.java files

builder --> genRepos : 3.3: generate_repositories()\n→ JpaRepository<Entity, UUID>\ninterfaces
genRepos --> fs : 3.4: write Repository.java files

builder --> genServices : 3.5: generate_services()\n→ @Service classes with\nCRUD methods
genServices --> fs : 3.6: write Service.java files

builder --> genControllers : 3.7: generate_controllers()\n→ @RestController with\n@GetMapping/@PostMapping etc.
genControllers --> fs : 3.8: write Controller.java files

builder --> genDtos : 3.9: generate_dtos()\n→ DTO classes
genDtos --> fs : 3.10: write Dto.java files

builder --> genPostman : 3.11: generate_postman()\n→ collection with folders\nper class + Health check
genPostman --> fs : 3.12: write postman_collection.json

builder --> templates : 3.13: render Jinja2 templates\n(pom.xml, application.properties,\nDemoApplication.java,\nHealthController.java,\nDockerfile, docker-compose.yml,\nREADME.md)
templates --> fs : 3.14: write template files

' === ZIP y descarga ===
router --> fs : 4: zip_generated_project(output_dir)
fs --> router : 4.1: zip_path
router --> axios : 4.2: FileResponse(zip_path)\nmedia_type="application/zip"
axios --> exportApi : 4.3: binary ZIP download
exportApi --> diagram : 4.4: trigger browser download\n"generated_project_{id}.zip"

' === Uso posterior (fuera del sistema) ===
user --> user : 5: unzip → cd project →\ndocker compose up -d --build\n(Spring Boot 8090 + Postgres 5434)

@enduml
